Chapter: EqGenericRecursive

  cites Foreword chapter Console

 COMPILER-43. A recursive sum's `==` never reached `emit-eq-op`:
 `lower-eq-dispatch` looked `__eq_<T>` up by NAME with the type arguments
 already dropped, so every instantiation of a parameterised recursive type
 shared one desugared helper whose field stayed at the declaration's own
 type variable, and a `tvar` operand falls through to a word compare on two
 heap pointers.

 Every row builds one side at RUNTIME with `integer-to-text`, so the two
 sides are separate allocations holding equal content; `text-control` is the
 check that the instrument itself is honest, because a pooled literal on
 both sides would compare equal by pointer for the wrong reason.

 `named-concrete` is the positive control: a recursive sum with a CONCRETE
 field compared structurally before this fix and must keep doing so.
 `pair-generic` is the non-recursive generic, which the inlining path
 already instantiated correctly.

 THE TWO-INSTANTIATION ROWS ARE THE POINT, and they are why the helper key
 carries the type arguments. Keyed on the bare sum name, `Box Text` and
 `Box Integer` share one helper: whichever instantiation is requested first
 builds it, and the other compares its field with the wrong routine --
 an Integer field handed to `__str_eq` reads a length and a payload out of
 an integer. `box-int-eq` and `box-int-ne` are that case, and they must
 disagree with each other or the helper is comparing pointers again.

Section: Types

  Pair a = | P (a) (a)

  Box a = | Empty | Cell (a) (Box a)

  Named = | Nil | Node (Text) (Named)

Section: Helpers

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("text-control   : " & yn ("12" == integer-to-text 12))
    print-line-uni ("named-concrete : " & yn (Node "12" Nil == Node (integer-to-text 12) Nil))
    print-line-uni ("pair-generic   : " & yn (P "12" "9" == P (integer-to-text 12) "9"))
    print-line-uni ("box-text-eq    : " & yn (Cell "12" Empty == Cell (integer-to-text 12) Empty))
    print-line-uni ("box-text-ne    : " & yn (Cell "12" Empty == Cell (integer-to-text 13) Empty))
    print-line-uni ("box-int-eq     : " & yn (Cell 12 Empty == Cell (6 + 6) Empty))
    print-line-uni ("box-int-ne     : " & yn (Cell 12 Empty == Cell (6 + 7) Empty))
    print-line-uni ("box-nested     : " & yn (Cell "12" (Cell "9" Empty) == Cell (integer-to-text 12) (Cell "9" Empty)))
    print-line-uni ("box-depth-ne   : " & yn (Cell "12" (Cell "9" Empty) == Cell "12" Empty))
  end

